            <persName type="full">Jean de Boschère</persName>
            <date type="birth" when="1878-07-05"/>
            <date type="death" when="1953-01-17"/>
            <note type="gender">M</note>
         </ab>
         <div type="bio">
            <p>Belgian artist and writer. During WWI he became associated with the Imagists and met <name type="person" key="poun85">Ezra Pound</name>, who helped to place his poems and drawings in <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">The Little Review</name>. Pound reported to JJ that Boschère expressed great praise for <name type="work" key="W_APORTRAIT">A Portrait of the Artist as a Young Man</name>. He visited JJ in Paris in June 1921 and was one of the signers of the 2 February 1927 letter of protest against <name type="person" key="roth93">Samuel Roth</name>’s publication of <name type="work" key="W_ULYSSES">Ulysses</name>. <hi rend="bold">William Brockman</hi>
                </p>
         </div>
